Both halves of this reference are generated from the same Zig declarations the
library compiles, and a build check fails when either goes stale, so what you
read here matches the code. For *which* surface to reach for and how to start,
see [Surfaces]($link.page('surfaces')); this page is the lookup.

## The Zig API

The [Zig API reference]($link.page('reference/api')) is generated from the public
`pancake` module on every site build. It is the exact surface a Zig consumer imports,
with the ownership and lifetime notes attached to the declarations that carry them.

## The C ABI

The C surface is a set of composable archives, and this table is the site's one
inventory of them. Each header is generated from the Zig declarations its
archive compiles.

| Archive | Header | What it carries |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `libpancake_ocapn` | [`pancake_ocapn.h`](https://codeberg.org/jimisaacs/pancake/src/branch/main/include/pancake_ocapn.h) | the sans-io peer and the shared vocabulary |
| `libpancake_driver` | [`pancake_driver.h`](https://codeberg.org/jimisaacs/pancake/src/branch/main/include/pancake_driver.h) | the byte-fed host tier (`pancake_host_*`) |
| `libpancake_net` | none; it appears in the link line only | the shared net core beneath every transport |
| `libpancake_net_transport_tcp` | [`pancake_net_transport_tcp.h`](https://codeberg.org/jimisaacs/pancake/src/branch/main/include/pancake_net_transport_tcp.h) | cleartext TCP |
| `libpancake_net_transport_inproc` | [`pancake_net_transport_inproc.h`](https://codeberg.org/jimisaacs/pancake/src/branch/main/include/pancake_net_transport_inproc.h) | in-process byte pipes, no sockets |
| `libpancake_net_transport_iroh` | [`pancake_net_transport_iroh.h`](https://codeberg.org/jimisaacs/pancake/src/branch/main/include/pancake_net_transport_iroh.h) | encrypted QUIC; optional, links the Rust sidecar |
| `libpancake_net_transport_webrtc` | [`pancake_net_transport_webrtc.h`](https://codeberg.org/jimisaacs/pancake/src/branch/main/include/pancake_net_transport_webrtc.h) | peer-to-peer WebRTC DataChannel; optional, links the Rust sidecar |

The driver and transport headers are companions, not supersets: each one
`#include`s `pancake_ocapn.h`, declares only its own family, and expects its
archive to be linked alongside `libpancake_ocapn`.
For the route from a build to a first complete C program, read
[consuming pancake from C](https://codeberg.org/jimisaacs/pancake/src/branch/main/docs/consuming-from-c.md).
